  "query_preview": "..\n\nThe rest of today through Friday..\n\nUpper level ridging will keep conditions warm and mostly dry\nthrough next week.\n\nA weak shortwave moving through the region will bring gusty winds\nover the western foothills again tonight into Sunday. Conditions \nwill be favorable for strong gap winds of 40 to 60 mph near \nLivingston as 700 mb winds turn out of the southwest and increase \nto 40 to 50 kts and a favorable pressure gradient sets up. As a \nresult, a Wind Advisory is in effect tonight into Sunday for the \nLivingston to Nye area. Over the rest of the western foothills, \ngusts of 30 to 45 mph will be common, potentially (25% chance) as \nfar east as Billings. As the shortwave moves across the region \nSunday, the plains will see occasional gusts around 20 to 30 mph.\n\nHigh temperatures will increase into Sunday, reaching the 60s to\nlow 70s. Then, a series of weak shortwaves late Sunday through\nTuesday will allow highs to fall towards the 50s and increase\ncloud cover. With the shortwaves, some isolated showers may\ndevelop, with the best chance (30%) over the mountains Tuesday.\n\nUpper level ridging looks to remain in place through at least\nFriday. Highs will increase again well above seasonable values\n(mid to upper 40s) to 60s to low 70s by the end of the work week.\nArcher",
